        "pkcontributionId": 64277,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 292,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>GA15.0 Polyp of cervix uteri</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T14:59:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64278,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 292,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> M&uuml;llerian papilloma of infancy</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> mesonephric papilloma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T14:59:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64279,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 292,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T14:59:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64280,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 292,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>M&uuml;llerian papilloma occurs in the upper vagina or cervix, usually posteriorly.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T14:59:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64281,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 292,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>M&uuml;llerian papilloma is associated with vaginal bleeding or discharge.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T14:59:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64282,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 292,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>M&uuml;llerian papilloma occurs almost exclusively in children, typically aged 2&ndash;5&nbsp;years, but it rarely arises in older individuals {26948653; 14043062}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T14:59:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64283,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 292,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T14:59:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64284,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 292,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T14:59:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64285,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 292,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>M&uuml;llerian papilloma is a friable polypoid or papillary frond-like cervical lesion, generally &lt;&nbsp;2&nbsp;cm {15708065}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T14:59:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64286,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 292,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Finely branching fibrous papillae are lined by a single layer of benign cuboidal to columnar epithelial cells. Squamous metaplasia or hobnail-type cells may be present, but cytology is bland, without atypia or mitotic activity {14043062; 26948653}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T14:59:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64287,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 292,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T14:59:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64288,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 292,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T14:59:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64289,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 292,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a cervical or upper vaginal exophytic lesion occurring in children; histologically, branching fibrous papillae lined by a single layer of benign glandular epithelium, with or without squamous metaplasia.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T14:59:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
